{
  "category": "inverter",
  "specs": {
    "class": {
      "definition": "Combined = inverter+MPPT+charger in one box; Standalone = inverter only (needs a separate charge controller)",
      "type": "enum",
      "values": [
        "all-in-one",
        "standalone"
      ]
    },
    "input_voltage": {
      "definition": "Battery/bus input voltage(s). A list means multi-voltage capable.",
      "unit": "V",
      "type": "number|list"
    },
    "continuous_w": {
      "definition": "Continuous output power",
      "unit": "W",
      "type": "number"
    },
    "surge_w": {
      "definition": "Peak/surge output power",
      "unit": "W",
      "type": "number"
    },
    "idle_w": {
      "definition": "No-load self-consumption (runs all day on a solar-direct build)",
      "unit": "W",
      "type": "number"
    },
    "mppt_builtin": {
      "definition": "Includes a solar MPPT charge controller",
      "type": "bool"
    },
    "pv_max_voltage": {
      "definition": "Max PV input voltage of the built-in MPPT (all-in-one only)",
      "unit": "V",
      "type": "number"
    },
    "output_ac_v": {
      "definition": "AC output voltage",
      "unit": "V",
      "type": "number"
    },
    "split_phase": {
      "definition": "Can output 120/240 V split-phase",
      "type": "bool"
    },
    "waveform": {
      "definition": "Output waveform (must be pure sine for AC compressors)",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "scale": {
      "definition": "Intended scale for this project",
      "type": "enum",
      "values": [
        "tent",
        "dwelling"
      ]
    },
    "price_usd": {
      "definition": "Approximate street price (verify)",
      "unit": "USD",
      "type": "number"
    },
    "source": {
      "definition": "Reference URL",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "mass_kg": {
      "definition": "Mass of one unit/block (feeds system_mass_kg)",
      "unit": "kg",
      "type": "number"
    },
    "efficiency": {
      "definition": "Peak battery->AC conversion efficiency (feeds inverter_conv_loss). Datasheet where available, else typical.",
      "unit": "fraction",
      "type": "number"
    },
    "mppt_efficiency": {
      "definition": "Peak PV->battery efficiency of built-in MPPT (all-in-one only). Datasheet/typical.",
      "unit": "fraction",
      "type": "number"
    }
  },
  "guidance": [
    "Only needed on the AC-inverter mini-split path; a native DC AC unit skips the inverter entirely.",
    "Must be pure sine wave (AC compressors and electronics require it).",
    "Two classes: Combined (all-in-one = inverter+MPPT+charger, simplest, higher idle, fixed PV window) vs Standalone (inverter only + a separate MPPT, more boxes, frugal idle, free MPPT choice).",
    "Bus-voltage coupling: a 2 kW load pulls ~170 A at 12 V, ~85 A at 24 V, ~42 A at 48 V. 12 V inverters cap ~2-3 kW and run hot; the best 2-3 kW and all-in-one units are 24 V or 48 V.",
    "Idle draw matters on a solar-direct daytime build (runs for hours; every 10 W idle ~= 80 Wh/day). Frugal: Victron Phoenix/MultiPlus ~8-15 W. Hungry: all-in-ones + AIMS ~25-70 W.",
    "The EG4 3000EHV is the all-in-one exception on PV: its 500 V input strings cheap 72-cell surplus panels like a good standalone MPPT would.",
    "Standalone system cost must add a separate MPPT (~$250-280) to compare apples-to-apples with an all-in-one."
  ],
